.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt GROWBOOT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm growboot
.Nd prepare a recovery environment from a boot-partition backup
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar BOOT.IMG ENV.IMG
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads a complete 64 MiB boot-partition backup from
.Ar BOOT.IMG
through the boot-slot library.
The saved 1024-byte GRUB environment must occupy one cluster.
.Pp
The editor makes recovery the saved boot entry and removes the trial
entry in a two-sector memory copy.
No write reaches
.Ar BOOT.IMG .
The resulting environment is written to
.Ar ENV.IMG ,
which is created exclusively.
An existing output path is refused, including the input path itself.
Standard output reports the environment's partition-relative sector.
.Pp
Recovery's 4 MiB RAM file system cannot hold the complete boot image.
.Nm
therefore prepares only the environment.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl growboot boot.img env.img
.Pp
In the source tree,
.Ql tests/run grow
exercises this command.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
An environment that does not occupy one cluster is reported as:
.Dl growboot: the saved environment must occupy one cluster
Failure to create a new output file is reported with
.Ql growboot: creating the new environment file
and the system error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr recovery 7 ,
.Xr bootctl 8 ,
.Xr growroot 8
